WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:00.995
Type light.

00:00:00.995 --> 00:00:03.447
One word, one row of a table, one arrow.

00:00:03.827 --> 00:00:04.431
Add dismiss.

00:00:04.431 --> 00:00:07.450
Its row weighs more, and the sum swings to dialog.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:08.981
Swap the two words.

00:00:08.981 --> 00:00:11.570
The arrows trade places, and the sum stays put.

00:00:13.998 --> 00:00:15.052
Hi, I'm Tindra!

00:00:15.052 --> 00:00:18.917
Chrome's Modern Web Guidance swapped a twenty-three megabyte transformer for a

00:00:18.917 --> 00:00:20.323
table and a sum.

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:24.807
The table has one row per word.

00:00:24.807 --> 00:00:28.052
Twenty-nine thousand words, two hundred fifty-six small integers each.

00:00:28.472 --> 00:00:30.609
A query lights up its words' rows.

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:31.525
Animate, height, auto.

00:00:31.945 --> 00:00:36.965
Each row is scaled by one number, its weight, and added into the output.

00:00:36.965 --> 00:00:39.117
Three words, seven hundred sixty-eight multiply-adds.

00:00:39.537 --> 00:00:41.895
Normalize it, and compare with every guide.

00:00:41.895 --> 00:00:45.263
The guides were embedded once, by Gemini, at release time.

00:00:46.975 --> 00:00:48.561
Every word gets a row.

00:00:48.561 --> 00:00:51.416
Fetch priority is one word here, not four fragments.

00:00:51.816 --> 00:00:56.686
Gemini embeds each word alone, and keeps the first two hundred fifty-six dimensions.

00:00:57.086 --> 00:00:58.665
Rare words get heavier weights.

00:00:59.686 --> 00:01:02.550
Then the rows are tuned, so word sums land where Gemini

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.592
puts the whole query.

00:01:03.992 --> 00:01:07.915
Last, each row is squeezed into bytes, its scale folded into its weight.

00:01:09.175 --> 00:01:13.177
On my M1 Max, the loop itself takes about one microsecond.

00:01:13.177 --> 00:01:17.178
A cold single call takes about twenty-five, close to Google's thirty.

00:01:18.383 --> 00:01:22.415
Replaying the public agent queries, the right guide is in the top

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:25.103
ten ninety-nine point four percent of the time.

00:01:25.103 --> 00:01:26.111
Exactly Google's number.

00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:32.118
But the out-of-scope set has ninety queries like jest mocks and Kubernetes.

00:01:32.538 --> 00:01:33.301
Rejected: none.

00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:35.209
Every one gets ten guides.

00:01:37.475 --> 00:01:42.290
For short queries against a frozen corpus, a distilled table does the transformer's job.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.353
Keep the teacher for the documents.

00:01:46.192 --> 00:01:50.049
A lookup and a sum, a microsecond of math, and one gate to fix.

00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:50.876
Thanks for watching!

00:01:51.296 --> 00:01:53.388
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:53.388 --> 00:01:53.985
I'm Tindra.

00:01:53.985 --> 00:01:54.284
Bye!
